<title>UK: CRICKET-ENGLAND V AUSTRALIA THIRD TEST SCOREBOARD.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLAND V AUSTRALIA THIRD TEST SCOREBOARD.</headline>
<dateline>MANCHESTER, England 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scoreboard on the</p>
<p>final day of the third cricket test between England and</p>
<p>Australia at Old Trafford on Monday:</p>
<p>Australia first innings 235 (S.Waugh 108; D.Headley 4-72,</p>
<p>D.Gough 3-52). Second innings 395-8 declared (S.Waugh 116)</p>
<p>England first innings 162 (M.Butcher 51; S.Warne 6-48,</p>
<p>G.McGrath 3-40)</p>
<p>England second innings (overnight 130-5)</p>
<p> M.Butcher c McGrath b Gillespie	28</p>
<p> M.Atherton lbw b Gillespie	     21</p>
<p> A.Stewart b Warne			   1</p>
<p> N.Hussain lbw b Gillespie		 1</p>
<p> G.Thorpe c Healy b Warne		  7</p>
<p> J.Crawley hit wicket b Mcgrath	 83</p>
<p> M.Ealham c Healy b McGrath		9</p>
<p> R.Croft c Reiffel b McGrath	     7</p>
<p> D.Gough b McGrath			   6</p>
<p> A.Caddick c Gillespie b Warne	  17</p>
<p> D.Headley not out			   0</p>
<p> Extras (b-14 lb-4 w-1 nb-1)	    20</p>
<p> Total (73.4 overs)			200</p>
<p>Fall of wickets: 1-44 2-45 3-50 4-55 5-84 6-158 7-170 8-177</p>
<p>9-188.</p>
<p>Bowling: McGrath 21-4-46-4, Gillespie 12-4-31-3, Reiffel</p>
<p>2-0-8-0, Warne 30.4-8-63-3, Bevan 8-2-34-0.</p>
<p>Result: Australia won by 268 runs</p>
<p>First test: Edgbaston, England won by nine wickets</p>
<p>Second test: Lord's, Match drawn</p>
<p>Fourth test: Headingley, Leeds July 24-28</p>
<p>Fifth test: Trent Bridge, Nottingham August 7-11</p>
<p>Sixth test: Oval, August 21-25</p>
</text>
